====Guess That Fusion Quiz Show====
On 2F, players can participate to "Guess That Fusion Quiz Show" and win Radio Points.

During the game, the player is shown the silhouette of a fusion sprite and must first guess which Pokémon is the body, then the head. Guessing incorrectly will then reveal the unobscured sprite and the player will have a second chance to guess the parts for less points. Correctly guessing multiple in a row will reward the player with bonus points.

There are two difficulty levels, Regular and Advanced. In Regular, the player is given a choice of 4 Pokémon to choose from, whereas in Advanced, the player must select from a list of all unfused Pokémon. The player can also choose between a game of 3, 5 or 10 rounds. At first the player can only play Regular difficulty with 3 rounds, but will unlock the other options after obtaining a score of 5,000 points in a single game (and unlocking the Teleporter).

After unlocking the difficulty and round options, the player can play again whenever they want and can earn more prizes for obtaining a certain amount of points in a single game. Higher tier rewards will be obtained in addition to the lower tier rewards (all can be earned in a single game).

