===Art Gallery===
In the western side of the city is an art gallery that each day on the first floor will have on display six works of art by a random spriter who has contributed [[Custom Sprites|fusion sprites]] to the game.

If the player has defeated the [[Elite Four]], then each day there is a 40% chance that the spriter will appear at the art gallery and can be battled. The spriter will use a random three of the Pokémon on display in the gallery, all matching the highest level in the player's party. If the player has entered the art gallery at least six times, then by talking to the gallery manager they will be able to choose a spriter to be featured the following [[Time|day]]. When the player chooses a custom spriter after having defeated the Elite Four, thit custom spriter is guaranteed to appear.

On the second floor of the art gallery, there will be random Team Flags on display, which the player can purchase for {{P$}}5,000 to use as their [[Character_Customization#Trainer_Card_Background|Trainer Card Background]]. On display in the middle of the second floor, will be the Half-million Milestone Banner, which the player can also purchase as a Trainer Card Background for {{P$}}10,000.

===Magnet Rise Move Tutor===
A Scientist in the train station will teach [[bulbapedia:Magnet Rise (move)|Magnet Rise]] to the player's Pokémon for {{P$}}1,500.

===Role Play Move Tutor===
The woman in the bottom right corner of the Radio Tower's 3rd floor will teach [[bulbapedia:Role Play (move)|Role Play]] to the player's Pokémon for {{P$}}1,500.

===Sabrina Rematch===
After defeating the [[Elite Four]], Sabrina can be found next to the Department Store during the [[Time|night]]. After talking to her, she will appear at the Fighting Arena in [[Vermillion City]] for a [[Gym Leader rematches|rematch]].

